course: dictionary
lesson: 15597
title: Tahitian: from Tahiti
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Tahitian is a word about a place, a people and a language. As an adjective, it describes something from or about Tahiti: «We ate Tahitian vanilla ice cream.» Here Tahitian tells you which vanilla it is.
explain: As a noun, a Tahitian is a person from Tahiti, and the plural is Tahitians: «The Tahitians welcomed the visitors with a dance.» A capital letter often tells you a word is a name for a place, people or language.
explain: Tahitian can also name the language spoken on Tahiti: «Maria speaks Tahitian with her grandmother.» Check the words around it. If the sentence is about talking, speaking or learning, Tahitian means the language.
fact: Tahiti is the largest island of French Polynesia, in the South Pacific Ocean.
fact: The Tahitian language is related to Māori and Hawaiian.
fact: Tahiti is a volcanic island with coral reefs around it.
fact: Captain James Cook visited Tahiti in 1769.
fact: The French painter Paul Gauguin painted Tahitian people and landscapes.
exercise: «The Tahitian dance was full of colour and rhythm.» What does Tahitian mean here? | A kind of cold drink | A sport played on ice | *From or about Tahiti | A type of volcano
exercise: What is a Tahitian? | A kind of coral | *A person from Tahiti | A large volcano | A French painter
exercise: «Tahitian is related to Māori and Hawaiian.» What is Tahitian in this sentence? | *A language spoken on Tahiti | A kind of pearl | A famous painter | A place in the Pacific
test: In which year did Captain James Cook visit Tahiti? | 1569 | 1969 | *1769 | 1869
test: In «The Tahitian pearl was pale and shiny», what kind of word is Tahitian? | A noun, because it names a person | A verb, because it shows an action | *An adjective, because it describes the pearl
exam: Which statement is true? | Tahiti is a country in Europe | Tahitian means very cold | *Tahitian can describe things, people or a language | Tahitian is always a person
